Hi,

Just a brief message for all newbies in this newsgroup, since there are
LOTS of questions lately that have been answered many times before
already, and are extensively described in the spoilers.

If you have any questions on NetHack, PLEASE try to get an answer from
the NetHack Spoilers Site first, before you ask it here. The answer
will usually be more extensive, more correct, and you'll have it faster
than when you have to wait until someone responds to your question over
here.

To get these spoilers, do the following:

	ftp ftp.krl.caltech.edu
	(usercode) anonymous
	(password) your own usercode	(not your password)
	cd /pub/nethack
	hash				(optional)
	binary				(NOT optional)
	get ALLFILES.ZIP
	quit

This will copy the file ALLFILES.ZIP to your own system. This file
contains all other files from the /pub/nethack directory on the krl ftp
site. If you want only specific files, or files from subdirectories,
get those in the same way you could have got the ALLFILES file above.

If you have no access to the ftp protocol, but you HAVE e-mail (which
you usually have if you can read the news), than you might want to try
the ftpmail server: make a message that just says "help", and send it
to ftpmail@decwrl.dec.com, and you'll be sent a file that tells you how
to get ftp-available files via mail.

I hope this will prevent a lot of unnecessary questions for a while...

